---
title: Current controller ownership and takeover
---
flowchart TD
  accTitle: One run owns input until revoked
  accDescr: A trusted caller acquires a process-local capability only with fresh normal-play evidence and empty queues. Its semantic action rechecks lease, admission generation and observed native authority. Competing external input is rejected. Observe, status and goal recording remain available. Pause and recovery revoke ownership, and native takeover, transport failures and shutdown invalidate it. Resume does not reacquire. Native commit cannot be undone. The run service is the trusted caller for explicitly admitted gameplay tasks.
  Caller[Trusted in-process caller] -->|Explicit acquire| Gate{Fresh normal play<br/>Empty writers and queues}
  Gate -->|Pass| Lease[Exact RunLease object]
  Gate -->|Fail| Reject[Reject without input]
  Lease -->|One semantic action| Check{Live lease and original generation<br/>Matching observation}
  Check -->|Pass| Native[Native token check at commit]
  Check -->|Fail| Reject
  External[External key, action, walk, resume] -->|While owned| Reject
  Operator[Pause, recovery or owner release] -->|Revoke before return| Revoke[No run owner]
  Invalidate[Native takeover, transport failures, shutdown] -->|Invalidate| Revoke
  Revoke -->|Reconcile or restart as needed<br/>Then successful Resume| Manual[Manual transport permission<br/>No run lease]
  Read[Observe, status, goal recording] -->|Available while owned| View[Evidence and descriptive status]
  Native --> Limit[Committed input cannot be undone]
